   "name": "planet-zoo",
   "title": "Planet Zoo",
   "summary": "Visit a flat showroom surface for any planet, with every tile, decorative, resource and entity its map generation can place laid out in labelled rows. Works with planet mods too. Admin-only by default; a map setting opens it to everyone.",
   "description": "**AI disclosure:** this mod was made with the help of AI (Claude by Anthropic).\r\n\r\n# Planet Zoo\r\n\r\n**See everything a planet can generate, all in one place.**\r\n\r\nPlanet Zoo builds a flat showroom surface for any planet. Every tile, decorative, resource, cliff and entity that the planet's map generation can place is laid out in neat, labelled rows. You can look at a whole planet's palette in a minute, without flying there or searching the map for that one rare rock.\r\n\r\nIt's useful for planet mod authors who want to check their map generation, and for anyone who wants to see what a modded planet has before going there.\r\n\r\n## 🤝 Requirements and compatibility\r\n\r\n- **Required:** Space Age\r\n- **Planet mods:** any planet with map generation shows up in the list automatically.\r\n- **Versions:** the 2.0 and 2.1 versions are released together with the same features (1.0.0 for Factorio 2.0 and 1.0.1 for Factorio 2.1). Factorio 2.1 adds new things to some vanilla planets, and the zoo shows them automatically.\r\n- **Existing saves:** can be added at any time. It doesn't change your normal surfaces, only adds its own zoo surfaces.\r\n- **Removing the mod:** go **Back** from any zoo first. The zoo surfaces stay in the save after the mod is removed.\r\n\r\n## 📝 What is not shown\r\n\r\n- Things placed by scripts instead of map generation (for example the Nauvis crash site) are not in the zoo.\r\n- Space platforms and asteroids have no map generation, so they have no zoo.\r\n\r\n## 🌐 Languages\r\n\r\n- English\r\n- Magyar (Hungarian)\r\n\r\n## 💬 Feedback\r\n\r\nIdeas, bug reports and suggestions are very welcome in the **Discussion** tab. If a modded planet's zoo looks wrong or is missing something, please tell me which mod it is!",
   "changelog": "---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVersion: 1.0.1\nDate: 23. 10. 2026\n  Info:\n    - Factorio 2.1 release of 1.0.0 with the same features.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVersion: 1.0.0\nDate: 23. 10. 2026\n  Features:\n    - A zoo surface for every planet: each tile, decorative, resource, cliff and entity its map generation places, in labelled rows.\n    - Works with planet mods: the list comes from each planet's map generation settings.\n    - Shortcut-bar button with a panel: visit any planet's zoo, rebuild it, or go back to where you were.\n    - /planet-zoo <planet> command; without a planet it opens the panel.\n    - Zoos are built on the first visit and deleted when the mod set changes, so they always match the loaded mods.\n  Settings:\n    - Everyone can use Planet Zoo (map, off by default). Off: admins only.\n  Locale:\n    - English and Hungarian.\n",
