   "name": "sulfur-everywhere",
   "title": "Sulfur Everywhere",
   "summary": "Enables sulfur mining on any planet of your choice. You can define a custom list of vanilla or modded planets in the startup settings.",
   "description": "**AI disclosure:** this mod was made with the help of AI (Claude by Anthropic).\r\n\r\n# Sulfur Everywhere\r\n\r\nHave you ever wanted to mine sulfur on other planets without relying solely on chemical processing? **Sulfur Everywhere** gives you the freedom to add mineable sulfur resource patches to your favorite planets in Factorio Space Age!\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n* **Simple Checkboxes:** No need to type internal planet names! Simply go to your Mod Settings and toggle sulfur generation on or off for each planet (Nauvis, Vulcanus, Gleba, Fulgora, Aquilo) using simple checkboxes.\r\n* **Starting Area Friendly:** Map generation is fully supported, and sulfur patches will spawn naturally, even in your starting areas.\r\n* **Map Generator Sliders:** Fully integrates with the map generator, adding the standard Frequency, Size, and Richness sliders for Sulfur on enabled planets.\r\n\r\n## Modded Planet Support\r\nCurrently, the mod includes toggle checkboxes for all official Space Age planets. **If you are playing with a mod that adds new custom planets and you'd like to mine sulfur there, just leave a comment/request in the discussion tab!** I will gladly add a built-in toggle for your requested planet in the next update.\r\n\r\n## How to use\r\n1. Go to **Settings -> Mod Settings -> Startup**.\r\n2. Find the **Sulfur on [Planet Name]** settings.\r\n3. Check the boxes for the planets where you want sulfur to spawn.\r\n4. Start a new game or explore new chunks on existing maps!",
